    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-fămĭlĭāris</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very intimate</i>, <i>very
				familiar</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perfamiliaris Philisto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Q.
					Fr. 2, 11</span></i>
			 (13), 4.—In tmesi: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phaedon Socrati per fuit familiaris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 18, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perfămĭlĭāris</span></b> ,
				is, m., <i>a very
				intimate</i> or <i>familiar friend</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 13, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Epicuri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 5, 31, 94</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">M. Antonii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Brut. 45, 168</span></i>
			.</div>
